\title{Summary of Work and Projects}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2025-09-03}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    Since early 2018 I have held various roles in crypto, working mostly in research and [formal verification](dhsorens-000X).
    My original interests in crypto were in consensus algorithms and formal verification frameworks for verifying smart contracts. When I started, those frameworks and tools were in their infancy, [K Framework](dhsorens-001D) being the only tool at the time to my knowledge that was production-ready for actual smart contracts.

    Over time, I became interested in the financial applications of [smart contracts](dhsorens-000Y) and I did my [PhD](dhsorens-phd) in verification strategies for financial [smart contracts](dhsorens-000W).

    Along the way, I became deeply interested in type theory and [proof assistants](dhsorens-000B), and these days am interested broadly in theorem-proving, [whether applied to software or formalized maths](dhsorens-notes).

    In my day-to-day, I still do a lot of work in the design, construction, and formal verification of smart contracts.
}

